    "result": "I implemented `RateLimiter` in `solution.py`, keeping the stub's class name and method signatures, and edited no other file. Each client has a deque of `(time, cost)` records, oldest first. Every public method first checks `now` against the limiter's largest time so far, and raises `ValueError` if it has gone backwards. Records with `now - t >= window_seconds` are dropped before counting, so a request exactly one window old no longer counts. `allow` records only when the request fits, so rejected calls use no budget. `remaining` is `limit` minus the live usage. `retry_after` returns `0.0` if the cost fits now; otherwise it walks the live records oldest first and returns how long until enough units expire. Argument checks follow the spec (integer `limit >= 1`, `window_seconds > 0`, `cost` from 1 to `limit`, `bool` rejected). I also reject non-numeric or NaN `now` values, which the spec does not mention. As instructed, I did not run or test the code.",
